    "body": "Ah actually, I put this into draft as triple checking against the spec and not just what I have written, also just realised that this is also unused but it probably should not be, since we're pushing the `<template>` on to the stack of open elements which means in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#insert-an-element-at-the-adjusted-insertion-location the adjusted location is recalculated a little late.\n\nThis was pre-existing based on the comment here: https://github.com/SerenityOS/serenity/blob/84d1758de3d52db53d7ea7fd81de78a5138ec932/Userland/Libraries/LibWeb/HTML/Parser/HTMLParser.cpp#L999\n\nI'll try adjust to fix that issue as well.",
